                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e43703c-cf59-367d-806f-029acc1b7833",
                        "entry_id": "e6a5837c-29e4-37fb-885c-8bb313297f12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Meerenge zwischen der chinesischen Provinz Fujian im Westen und der Insel Taiwan (früher Formosa) im Osten"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5722a1bc-f514-420d-8cbb-f6265cfb37e3",
                                "sense_id": "1e43703c-cf59-367d-806f-029acc1b7833",
                                "text": "„Nach der Fahrt eines US-Kriegsschiffs durch die Taiwanstraße reagieren die chinesischen Streitkräfte mit scharfer Kritik an den Vereinigten Staaten.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6c489ef3-c4b0-4193-ab20-851a1601c2c0",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6a5837c-29e4-37fb-885c-8bb313297f12",
                        "source_sense_id": "1e43703c-cf59-367d-806f-029acc1b7833",
                        "source_sense_description": "Meerenge zwischen der chinesischen Provinz Fujian im Westen und der Insel Taiwan",
                        "target_lang_word": "Taiwan Strait",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Taiwan Strait",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84a922ed-ad22-30a8-a46f-401be719555d",
                                        "entry_id": "41084fff-7ebc-35e8-b0bc-2c8f3671b196",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The strait dividing mainland Asia (incl. mainland China) from Taiwan island and connecting the East and South China Seas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f438a5a7-e87f-4c6e-86ef-88b3e7614aea",
                                                "sense_id": "84a922ed-ad22-30a8-a46f-401be719555d",
                                                "text": "Formosa (Taiwan) is an island located about 200 miles north of the Philippine Islands, and separated from the southeastern coast of China by Taiwan Strait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b0af026-db18-4779-8d96-2df52282bdea",
                                                "sense_id": "84a922ed-ad22-30a8-a46f-401be719555d",
                                                "text": "This Nation, which has fundamental commitments to the Republic of China, has for many years sought the renunciation of force in the Taiwan Strait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c248754f-4f56-4203-9687-5d1d74ae16cc",
                                                "sense_id": "84a922ed-ad22-30a8-a46f-401be719555d",
                                                "text": "Kinmen now supplies fully a third of Taiwan’s kaolin and feldspar need. A total of 40,000 tons of kaolin and 4,200 tons of feldspar will be shipped across the Taiwan Strait this year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "970749c0-4761-4d02-8c75-90c147ba8940",
                                                "sense_id": "84a922ed-ad22-30a8-a46f-401be719555d",
                                                "text": "Taipei lies on the east bank of the Tan-shui river between the mouths of two of its tributaries, the Hsin-tien and the Chi-lung. These rivers drain a fertile and humid basin surrounded by mountains on all sides but the northwest, where the Tan-shui flows into the Taiwan Straits facing the mainland."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9229cf51-b074-4880-927a-2035dc2199c9",
                                                "sense_id": "84a922ed-ad22-30a8-a46f-401be719555d",
                                                "text": "It was New Year's Eve, and the eighteen American officials who had hurriedly gathered in the State Department Operations Room on 31 December 1970, were still sharply divided after four hours of discussion.¹ The issue was what, if anything, the Seventh Fleet should do in the event of Chinese naval action against the U.S. seismic survey vessels then beginning to explore for oil in disputed waters of the East China Sea, the Taiwan Strait, and the Yellow Sea."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f0ffb1d-f06d-4a42-afbf-1cfe21d62c4d",
                                                "sense_id": "84a922ed-ad22-30a8-a46f-401be719555d",
                                                "text": "China liked the Taiwanese investment, but could not agree to give up its claim to sovereignty over the island; finding the right balance between economic pragmatism and aggressive nationalism was a constant challenge for China's leaders, especially during election season in Taiwan. I thought China had gone too far with the missile tests, and quickly, but without fanfare, I ordered a carrier group from the U.S. Navy's Pacific fleet to sail to the Taiwan Strait. The crisis passed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "16484be4-5bfa-4e07-8f38-2154ed6d96f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6a5837c-29e4-37fb-885c-8bb313297f12",
                        "source_sense_id": "1e43703c-cf59-367d-806f-029acc1b7833",
                        "source_sense_description": "Meerenge zwischen der chinesischen Provinz Fujian im Westen und der Insel Taiwan",
                        "target_lang_word": "Formosa Strait",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Formosa Strait",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7c466e0-e2d4-337d-bd98-536b1d8dff11",
                                        "entry_id": "5204e0bc-08b0-3c23-ad37-b8e58d3ae588",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of Taiwan Strait."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c0f1528-9455-49d8-927c-d652b25cbcad",
                                                "sense_id": "a7c466e0-e2d4-337d-bd98-536b1d8dff11",
                                                "text": "The line beyond which American pilots do not fly in the troubled Formosa Strait area is called the “Davis Line” in honor of Brig. Gen. Benjamin O. Davis Jr., former commander of the 13th Provisional Air Force, stationed on Formosa[.] The mythical line is an undisclosed number of miles off the coast of Red China."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d186624b-d66d-4066-be94-f3db02a41d14",
                                                "sense_id": "a7c466e0-e2d4-337d-bd98-536b1d8dff11",
                                                "text": "In the Formosa Strait in 1955 we refused to retreat, and the enemy, true to his formula, for a while tried harassment but refused to attack. The crisis had cooled; it would not heat up again for three years.\nThe hard way is to have the courage to be patient."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f9d2915-8c99-4295-ac44-74696495d22e",
